A '''Scatha''' is a mob that has a chance to spawn when mining {{Item|Hard Stone}} in the [[Crystal Hollows]]. 

== Spawning ==
A {{MobSprite|Stoneworm}} or '''Scatha''' has a {{Chance|0.167%|1|600}} chance to spawn mining {{Item|Hard Stone}} in the [[Crystal Hollows]].
<!-- These are conclusions based on in-game tests conducted on 13 August 2025. Please correct accordingly if you observe conflicting behavior. -->
<!-- Standing in a tunnel with any of the blocks to the sides or above player removed seems to prevent spawning, though an element of chance causes results of these tests to not be 100% reliable. Testing in case of removing the block below is, obviously, problematic. -->
<!-- Based off my own testing the blocks or air left, right, and above your chosen two rows of blocks do not appear to factor into the spawning conditions. Nor do the blocks broken need to be hard stone, I've spawned them off mithril. 
 Love, Sci.-->
There is an {{Chance|80%|4|5}} chance for the spawned mob to be a {{MobSprite|Stoneworm}}, and a {{Chance|20%|1|5}} chance for a '''Scatha''' to spawn. There is a {{Green|30s}} cooldown after a '''Scatha''' or {{MobSprite|Stoneworm}} spawns.

Chance to spawn {{MobSprite|Stoneworm}}s can be increased with {{Reforge|Blazing}} reforge, [[Heart of the Mountain#Tunnel Vision|Tunnel Vision HotM]] perk and [[Marigold#Treasure of the Earth|Treasure of the Earth Gold Essence Shop]] perk. Chance to replace {{MobSprite|Stoneworm}}s with {{MobSprite|Scatha}}s can be increased with {{stat|tracking}}.

The {{Item|Armadillo Pet}} and {{AN|Mole}} perk do not prevent spawning by themselves, however the conditions mentioned above must still be met.

After digging out a suitable tunnel, breaking the blocks at the player's eye level on the side can still trigger '''Scathas''' spawning. Breaking the blocks below foot level will also spawn '''Scathas'''.

While spawning, '''Scathas''' make a unique squelching sound {{Green|3}} times, alerting players of their presence. Additionally, the following message appears in chat:
{{Dialogue|&7&oYou hear the sound of something approaching...}}

== Behavior ==
A '''Scatha''' slowly slithers through the tunnel it spawned in, turning back if it hits a block or gets too far away. It has {{Stat|health|10}}. They start off with a chain of {{Green|10}} segments, which decrease by one each time they are hit until killed. Each hit deals {{HP|1}} of damage to the '''Scatha'''.

If no blocks are present under the '''Scatha''' when it moves, the '''Scatha''' will float through the air. It does not go up or down and stays true to the Y-Axis it spawns at.

